+## OpenCode TRL Post-Training Review Lane
+
+Use OpenCode only as a bounded reviewer/helper for TRL post-training scripts, configs, tests, and runbook artifacts:
+
+- Good fits: review SFT/DPO/PPO/GRPO script structure, dataset formatting code, reward-model scaffolds, training argument sanity checks, tiny synthetic examples, and README/runbook drafts.
+- Hermes remains responsible for GPU/RAM checks, model/license selection, dataset privacy classification, reward/preference data handling, and the decision to start any run.
+- Do not send API keys, HF tokens, W&B keys, private preference data, proprietary prompts, human feedback records, generated checkpoints, or gated model credentials to OpenCode.
+- Do not let OpenCode launch training/RL loops, install heavyweight GPU packages, download large models, push checkpoints, or run expensive evals without explicit limits.
+- After OpenCode output, Hermes must run syntax checks and prefer tiny synthetic CPU/lightweight smokes before recommending full post-training.
